  "chapter": {
    "number": 18,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(19) For the end, a Psalm of David."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The heavens declare the glory of God; and the firmament proclaims the work of his hands.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Day to day",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 34
          },
          {
            "text": "utters speech, and night to night proclaims knowledge.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "There are no speeches or words,",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 35
          },
          {
            "text": "in which their voices are not heard.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Their voice is gone out into all the earth, and their words to the ends of the world.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "In the sun he has set his tabernacle; and he comes forth as a bridegroom out of his chamber: he will exult as a giant to run his course.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "His going forth is from the extremity of heaven, and his",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 36
          },
          {
            "text": "circuit to the other end of heaven: and no one shall be hidden from his heat.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The law of the Lord is",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 37
          },
          {
            "text": "perfect, converting souls: the testimony of the Lord is faithful, instructing babes.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The ordinances of the Lord are right, rejoicing the heart: the commandment of the Lord is bright, enlightening the eyes.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The fear of the Lord is pure, enduring for ever and ever: the judgments of the Lord are true, and justified altogether.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "To be desired more than gold, and much precious stone: sweeter also than honey and the honey-comb.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For your servant keeps to them: in the keeping of them there is great reward.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Who will understand his transgressions? purge you me from my secret sins.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 13,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And spare your servant the attack of strangers: if they do not gain the dominion over me, then shall I be blameless, and I shall be clear from great sin.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 14,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "So shall the sayings of my mouth, and the meditation of my heart, be pleasing continually before you, O Lord my helper, and my redeemer.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
